###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion. Remember that opposite sides of rectangles have the same lengths.

$\dfrac{\maroonD{LI}}{TY}=\dfrac{NI}{LY}$

We picked side $\maroonD{\overline{LI}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{TY}$ because it corresponds to side $\maroonD{\overline{LI}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides where we already knew the measurements.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle LIN
\\
{\text{short} \atop \text{leg}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\maroonD{LI}}{TY}=\dfrac{NI}{LY}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{long} \atop \text{leg}}
\\
&\triangle LYT
\end{array}$
